Fix a real upstream build bug (not an AXOS feature): release/src/router/Makefile
adds `-I$(HND_SRC)/bcmdrivers/opensource/include/bcm963xx
-I$(HND_SRC)/shared/opensource/include/bcm963xx` to the globally-exported
CFLAGS only when RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD is "y" — but httpd/web.c (via
userspace/public/include/bcm_imgutil_api.h, which #includes bcmTag.h)
needs the latter path unconditionally; nothing about that include is
hostapd-specific. Same shape of bug as 0003 (sys_util/gen_util),
0004/0006 (hostapd_config_6e.o and its support symbols): a downstream
dependency incidentally wired up only under RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD, when the
code that actually needs it has nothing to do with hostapd.

Confirmed via a real build attempt: `make gt-ax6000` (RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD
genuinely off) fails compiling httpd/web.o with "fatal error: bcmTag.h: No
such file or directory".

Fix: move just the bcm963xx include-path addition out of the
RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD block, so it's always exported. Left -DCONFIG_HOSTAPD
and the other genuinely hostapd-specific CFLAGS/exports (bcmcrypto include,
IEEE1905SOURCE_DIR, WPSSOURCE_DIR, LIBNL_DIR, WPA_SUPPLICANT_DIR, etc.)
gated as before.

`git apply --check`-verified against the pinned tag (3004.388.9), applied on
top of 0001-0008. Not yet verified past that point in a completed build —
see docs/build-environment.md and docs/ROADMAP.md.

diff --git a/release/src/router/Makefile b/release/src/router/Makefile
index fe6950ea62..e9b0032e00 100644
--- a/release/src/router/Makefile
+++ b/release/src/router/Makefile
@@ -484,10 +484,18 @@ CEVENT_APP_DIR := $(BASEDIR)/components/apps/cevent_app
 export CFLAGS += -D__CONFIG_BCM_CEVENT__ -DBCM_CEVENT -DBCM_CEVENTD
 export CONFIG_BCM_CEVENT=y
 endif
+# httpd/web.c (via userspace/public/include/bcm_imgutil_api.h) needs
+# bcmTag.h from shared/opensource/include/bcm963xx unconditionally — not
+# hostapd-specific — but this include path was only ever added when
+# RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD is "y". Confirmed via a real build attempt:
+# "fatal error: bcmTag.h: No such file or directory" compiling web.o.
+# Moved out of the RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD block below so it's always on the
+# include path, matching the same "downstream dependency wrongly coupled to
+# the feature flag" shape as 0003/0004/0006.
+export CFLAGS += -I$(HND_SRC)/bcmdrivers/opensource/include/bcm963xx -I$(HND_SRC)/shared/opensource/include/bcm963xx
 ifeq ($(RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD),y)
 export CFLAGS += -DCONFIG_HOSTAPD
 export CFLAGS += -I$(SRCBASE)/include -I$(SRCBASE)/../components/bcmcrypto/include
-export CFLAGS += -I$(HND_SRC)/bcmdrivers/opensource/include/bcm963xx -I$(HND_SRC)/shared/opensource/include/bcm963xx
 export IEEE1905SOURCE_DIR := $(BASEDIR)/components/apps/ieee1905
 export WPSSOURCE_DIR := $(BASEDIR)/components/apps/wps
 export LIBNL_DIR := $(BASEDIR)/components/opensource/router_tools/libnl
